lazykimi-plugin
===============

Kimi-native evidence-led agent workflow harness.

This work is a port of the LazyBuddy and LazyTrae harness designs to the
Kimi Code CLI platform, with lazycodex/OmO as the canonical design reference.

Upstream attribution
--------------------

LazyBuddy  -- https://github.com/elvinzhao10/LazyBuddy
  Bash/Python evidence-led agent workflow harness for CodeBuddy.
  Original author: elvinzhao10
  License: MIT

LazyTrae  -- https://github.com/elvinzhao10/LazyTrae
  Node.js evidence-led agent workflow harness for Trae IDE/Work/CLI.
  Original author: elvinzhao10
  License: MIT

lazycodex / OmO  -- https://github.com/code-yeongyu/lazycodex
  Canonical TypeScript distribution for Codex, wrapping OmO (oh-my-openagent).
  Provides the canonical ultrawork directive, agent role definitions, and
  component isolation patterns.
  Original author: code-yeongyu
  License: MIT

Kimi Code CLI  -- https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/kimi-code-cli/
  Target host platform. Provides SKILL.md system, 16 hook events,
  /swarm (300-agent swarm), /goal (persistent autonomous goals),
  /plan mode, MCP support, and plugin system.

This package reuses architectural patterns, skill structures, agent role
definitions, hook semantics, and verification contracts from the three
upstream projects. All ported content has been adapted to the Kimi Code CLI
platform's native capabilities and is distributed under the same MIT license.
